{"conditionalSetIds":[],"forecasterId":"demographics-ai-2036:run1:labor:audit","informationSetArtifactId":"sha256:3b332edfc9b8e305663203395ccfb21fff1e30f4b2369b0e31137a07fc254b60","modelForecastIds":[],"modelUse":"none","prediction":{"kind":"binary","positiveOutcomeId":"yes","probability":0.24},"questionHash":"sha256:cfe468fa9439bedeee3804a35583667745f13831322e2c91a89c02a1b211413b","questionId":"demographics-ai-2036-cq5","questionVersion":"1.0.0","rationale":"RESOLVING SERIES. ICE BofA MOVE Index (daily, never revised, but methodologically mutable — it was reweighted in 2019 and ICE can reconstitute or discontinue it; \"average\" of daily closes is unstated but immaterial). MSCI World (USD; price index vs net total return unstated). A GDP-weighted G7 10y nominal yield aggregate, which is analyst-constructed.\n\nCONJUNCT A: MOVE 10-year average >= 105. History: 2003-07 ~90-100; 2010-19 ~75-85; 2020 ~90; 2022-23 ~120-140; 2024 ~95-105; 2025-26 ~80-95. CRITICAL INDEX-CONSTRUCTION POINT: MOVE is NORMALISED (basis-point) implied vol on 1m options across 2/5/10/30y, so its LEVEL scales with the level of yields. A persistent 4%+ nominal regime floors MOVE around 85-100 without any stress; a 105 decade-average then requires 2022-23 conditions roughly a third of the time. 2A's plumbing facts (eroding convenience yields, levered basis-trade absorption, $1.4T circular AI commitments on ~$650B debt) support that. Marginal A = 0.48.\n\nCONJUNCT B, decomposed. (i) At least one MSCI World >=25% peak-to-trough drawdown in a 10-year window: reference class 1973-74, 1980-82, 1987, 2000-02, 2007-09, 2020, 2022 — ~7 episodes in 53 years, per-decade P(>=1) ~0.78-0.85; the USD denomination (a dollar rally deepens the measured drawdown) and a price-index rather than total-return basis each make 25% EASIER, +3 to 5pp; with the IMF's explicit 20% AI-led valuation shock scenario, 0.80. (ii) Conditional on that, yields FAIL to fall 50bp or rise 25bp in the window: historically G7 yields rally